(inspiring music)

00:01:02.465 --> 00:01:04.175
- Do you remember the first time

00:01:04.175 --> 00:01:06.305
that the thought of
fighting Floyd Mayweather

00:01:06.305 --> 00:01:07.805
crossed your mind?

00:01:09.355 --> 00:01:13.105
- Its been on my radar
for a long, long time.

00:01:14.747 --> 00:01:18.043
As a young man coming up in the game,

00:01:18.043 --> 00:01:20.390
in the sport of MMA,
I was listening to him

00:01:20.390 --> 00:01:24.137
in a similar weight class,
similar weight category

00:01:24.137 --> 00:01:26.005
speaking ill of the sport, speaking ill

00:01:26.005 --> 00:01:28.318
of the discipline, and as
a young kid I'm looking

00:01:28.318 --> 00:01:30.236
at him at such a high
level, saying these things

00:01:30.236 --> 00:01:31.763
about the sport that
I'm dedicating my entire

00:01:31.763 --> 00:01:33.444
life to, and I'm thinking,

00:01:33.444 --> 00:01:34.746
"I'll see you for that one day."

00:01:34.746 --> 00:01:36.791
- Why are we getting ready to watch

00:01:36.791 --> 00:01:38.681
Floyd "Money" Mayweather in the ring

00:01:38.681 --> 00:01:41.498
against Conor McGregor August 26th?

00:01:41.498 --> 00:01:44.498
- Man, it's what the world demanded.

00:01:46.071 --> 00:01:48.901
I put myself in the right position

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:50.311
to make it happen.

00:01:50.311 --> 00:01:52.041
So I put myself in the right position,

00:01:52.041 --> 00:01:55.111
to make it happen, it's all about chess.

00:01:55.111 --> 00:01:58.211
And its not really about
being on the chess board

00:01:58.211 --> 00:02:01.581
anymore, it's about
controlling the chess board.

00:02:01.581 --> 00:02:03.691
And that's what I was able to do.

00:02:03.691 --> 00:02:06.211
- Did you want this
fight, or did you respond

00:02:06.211 --> 00:02:08.461
to somebody who wanted you?

00:02:10.511 --> 00:02:13.041
- Actually, I asked for the fight.

00:02:13.041 --> 00:02:15.541
I think it was kind of mutual.

00:02:16.468 --> 00:02:19.218
I think I wanted the fight.

00:02:19.218 --> 00:02:21.885
Pretty sure he wanted the fight.

00:02:22.941 --> 00:02:26.531
I don't think in the beginning Dana White

00:02:26.531 --> 00:02:28.780
thought the fight could happen.

00:02:28.780 --> 00:02:30.467
But, we're here now.

00:02:30.467 --> 00:02:32.800
- You wanted the fight. Why?

00:02:34.825 --> 00:02:37.361
Not just because its
what the people wanted,

00:02:37.361 --> 00:02:39.768
I know, I got that answer, but what else?

00:02:39.768 --> 00:02:43.535
- Of course. I can put
myself in the position

00:02:43.535 --> 00:02:46.035
to make nine figures, why not?

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:50.491
Why not? So I put myself in the position.

00:02:50.491 --> 00:02:52.521
- Once again, there
will never be a fighter

00:02:52.521 --> 00:02:54.104
that's on my level.

00:02:55.071 --> 00:02:58.401
Because you have to be able
to go where I go mentally.

00:02:58.401 --> 00:03:00.771
You've got to be on my level mentally.

00:03:00.771 --> 00:03:03.461
And it's hard for anyone
to be on my level mentally.

00:03:03.461 --> 00:03:05.061
Because I think outside the box.

00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:06.961
That's why I'm always doing
record breaking numbers.

00:03:06.961 --> 00:03:09.041
That's why I'm always doing
record breaking things.

00:03:09.041 --> 00:03:11.757
That's why I was able to go
on Dancing With the Stars

00:03:11.757 --> 00:03:15.332
and take chances, and
go on WWE and still fans

00:03:15.332 --> 00:03:18.312
from the WWE are still fans
from Dancing with the Stars

00:03:18.312 --> 00:03:21.672
and take chances, to
become a household name.

00:03:21.672 --> 00:03:23.802
To become a pay-per-view star,

00:03:23.802 --> 00:03:25.892
to become a mega-superstar,

00:03:25.892 --> 00:03:29.475
to have the biggest
deal in sports history.

00:03:31.062 --> 00:03:33.872
I roll the dice. I take chances.

00:03:33.872 --> 00:03:36.602
- When you hear boxing
aficionados like Max Kellerman

00:03:36.602 --> 00:03:39.392
say you're not going to land a punch

00:03:39.392 --> 00:03:41.442
how do you react to that.

00:03:41.442 --> 00:03:44.872
Like today, we posted videos
of you hitting the bag,

00:03:44.872 --> 00:03:47.252
and its all people saying,
"Look how slow he is

00:03:47.252 --> 00:03:48.662
he doesn't know what he's doing.

00:03:48.662 --> 00:03:50.212
Look at this movement stuff."

00:03:50.212 --> 00:03:52.402
Do you enjoy that? Is that better for you?

00:03:52.402 --> 00:03:56.739
- It happens to all
greats, training methods.

00:03:56.739 --> 00:03:58.974
Everything is criticized.

00:03:58.974 --> 00:04:01.982
Originally Floyd, way
back, his method of hitting

00:04:01.982 --> 00:04:04.412
the pads and hitting
the bag was ridiculed.

00:04:04.412 --> 00:04:06.692
During the Hatten buildup,
what I started seeing

00:04:06.692 --> 00:04:09.633
about Floyd, they ridiculed his methods.

00:04:09.633 --> 00:04:11.433
And all of a sudden everyone starts trying

00:04:11.433 --> 00:04:12.653
to follow his methods.

00:04:12.653 --> 00:04:14.043
You know what I mean?

00:04:14.043 --> 00:04:15.943
When there's success,
it's been the same with me

00:04:15.943 --> 00:04:17.313
when I started incorporating
movement training,

00:04:17.313 --> 00:04:18.863
I started incorporating certain attacks,

00:04:18.863 --> 00:04:21.893
and certain approaches in
the mixed martial arts game.

00:04:21.893 --> 00:04:24.283
Ridiculed, it's a joke, a joker.

00:04:24.283 --> 00:04:27.133
How many times have I been
called a joke or a joker?

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:29.003
And then, everyone starts following,

00:04:29.003 --> 00:04:31.563
and trying to study,
it's no different here.

00:04:31.563 --> 00:04:33.363
The boxing game, oh look he doesn't

00:04:33.363 --> 00:04:34.968
move this way, what's he doing,

00:04:34.968 --> 00:04:36.076
this that and the other.

00:04:36.076 --> 00:04:39.860
They just don't understand,
they don't understand,

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:41.737
they just try and discard it.

00:04:41.737 --> 00:04:44.485
But thankfully, August 26th, there can be

00:04:44.485 --> 00:04:46.068
no running from it.

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:51.259
The same thing will happen
that always happens.

00:04:51.259 --> 00:04:52.659
They will try and push it away,

00:04:52.659 --> 00:04:55.069
it will be put in front of them.

00:04:55.069 --> 00:04:57.049
Floyd will be slapped,
and then they'll begin

00:04:57.049 --> 00:04:59.609
the studying process,
and then the implementing

00:04:59.609 --> 00:05:03.242
process, and then I'm on to the next.

00:05:03.242 --> 00:05:04.463
- Which is what?

00:05:04.463 --> 00:05:07.953
- I'm on to my next wave of preparation.

00:05:07.953 --> 00:05:09.373
So they're here, and I'm here again.

00:05:09.373 --> 00:05:10.843
And then I'm here, and then I'm here.

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:12.228
Do you understand what I'm saying?

00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:13.493
- Yeah.

00:05:13.493 --> 00:05:14.983
- So that's life.

00:05:14.983 --> 00:05:18.234
- A man that has never
been in the boxing ring

00:05:18.234 --> 00:05:21.134
is in the ring with the best ever.

00:05:21.134 --> 00:05:23.864
That's what you describe
yourself as being.

00:05:23.864 --> 00:05:26.764
- I don't describe myself, we must realize

00:05:26.764 --> 00:05:29.459
men lie, women lie, numbers don't lie.

00:05:29.459 --> 00:05:30.387
- 49 and 0.

00:05:30.387 --> 00:05:32.684
- Not just 49 and 0,
let's really talk about

00:05:32.684 --> 00:05:35.964
Mayweather who didn't broke
every record in boxing.

00:05:35.964 --> 00:05:38.104
When we get to talk about highest gate,

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:39.844
even right now they're saying,

00:05:39.844 --> 00:05:41.994
"Oh, a Mayweather fight didn't sell out."

00:05:41.994 --> 00:05:44.684
You know, when they do sell out, I think

00:05:44.684 --> 00:05:46.184
I reached the one,

00:05:47.624 --> 00:05:49.774
live gate it reached
like, 80 something million

00:05:49.774 --> 00:05:52.764
for this fight, already
we're at 60 something million

00:05:52.764 --> 00:05:54.538
though they're saying that Mayweather

00:05:54.538 --> 00:05:56.955
is not doing numbers anymore.

00:06:00.528 --> 00:06:02.448
As far as taking the less punishment,

00:06:02.448 --> 00:06:05.278
I've took less punishment
than any fighter.

00:06:05.278 --> 00:06:08.958
Not just best defense,
let's talk about offense.

00:06:08.958 --> 00:06:12.125
The most accurate fighter of all time.

00:06:13.438 --> 00:06:15.512
On the outside of the ring, it's not just

00:06:15.512 --> 00:06:17.393
about being inside of the ring.

00:06:17.393 --> 00:06:19.443
I've already conquered that.

00:06:19.443 --> 00:06:22.110
I'm even smarter on the outside.

00:06:24.236 --> 00:06:27.383
I have to be a genius to
even make a fight like this

00:06:27.383 --> 00:06:30.643
happen, so what does that say about me,

00:06:30.643 --> 00:06:32.283
for making this fight happen?

00:06:32.283 --> 00:06:34.523
- It says that you're a
brilliant businessman,

00:06:34.523 --> 00:06:35.743
not just a great boxer.

00:06:35.743 --> 00:06:38.113
- And that's what I always spoke about,

00:06:38.113 --> 00:06:39.823
that's what I always spoke about.

00:06:39.823 --> 00:06:42.723
I get my credit by what I do in the ring.

00:06:42.723 --> 00:06:44.353
But I don't get my credit

00:06:44.353 --> 00:06:46.353
about what I do on the outside.

00:06:46.353 --> 00:06:49.203
- You're enjoying great
riches and success now,

00:06:49.203 --> 00:06:51.143
but can you put yourself in the mindset

00:06:51.143 --> 00:06:52.333
of the guy who is waiting

00:06:52.333 --> 00:06:53.433
in line with other people.

00:06:53.433 --> 00:06:55.492
Do you remember what
that guy was thinking?

00:06:55.492 --> 00:06:56.325
- Always.

00:06:56.325 --> 00:06:57.583
- Were you daydreaming of this?

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.003
Was that even possible to daydream?

00:06:59.003 --> 00:07:00.709
- Every second of every
day I was daydreaming it.

00:07:00.709 --> 00:07:02.709
But of course I can go
back and think there.

00:07:02.709 --> 00:07:05.759
I lived there in my head
and I'll always be there.

00:07:05.759 --> 00:07:07.499
I show up and walk every single day

00:07:07.499 --> 00:07:09.129
like I'm not in the position I'm in.

00:07:09.129 --> 00:07:12.369
I'm not me, that's the mindset I'm having.

00:07:12.369 --> 00:07:13.729
It's walking.

00:07:13.729 --> 00:07:15.479
- You've got fighters

00:07:17.229 --> 00:07:19.609
that may be faster than me.

00:07:19.609 --> 00:07:21.599
You've got fighters

00:07:21.599 --> 00:07:23.932
that may hit harder than me.

00:07:24.989 --> 00:07:28.406
You've got fighters that's very athletic.

00:07:29.599 --> 00:07:30.939
But you don't have no fighter that

00:07:30.939 --> 00:07:34.159
can make adjustments like me.

00:07:34.159 --> 00:07:38.326
You don't have fighters that
can be on my level mentally.

00:07:40.449 --> 00:07:43.389
It's never personal for me.

00:07:43.389 --> 00:07:45.139
It's always business.

00:07:48.449 --> 00:07:52.339
Every other fighter
fights for certain things.

00:07:52.339 --> 00:07:55.709
Everybody fights for what they fight for.

00:07:55.709 --> 00:07:59.089
My thing is this: I keep
my eyes on the prize.

00:07:59.089 --> 00:08:01.649
I never focus on things outside the ring.

00:08:01.649 --> 00:08:05.149
My focus is the guy that's in front of me.

00:08:06.029 --> 00:08:08.099
You get to where you're trying to get to

00:08:08.099 --> 00:08:12.016
by staying focused,
staying on a parallel path.

00:08:13.009 --> 00:08:16.029
I always had a dream, and my dream

00:08:16.029 --> 00:08:17.612
was to be the best.

00:08:19.589 --> 00:08:22.256
No matter what happens Saturday,

00:08:24.479 --> 00:08:26.679
when it comes down to boxing,

00:08:26.679 --> 00:08:28.109
I'm the best at this.

00:08:28.109 --> 00:08:29.047
- What do you think they'll say

00:08:29.047 --> 00:08:31.697
about you in 50 years?

00:08:31.697 --> 00:08:33.547
- You know, I'm not quite sure what

00:08:33.547 --> 00:08:34.767
